# Backend Rules

- Keep backend code in TypeScript/Node service patterns (`routes`, `services`, `models`, `middleware`, `lib`, `filters`, `features`).
- Use `camelCase` for files/functions/variables and `PascalCase` for classes/interfaces.
- Do not introduce frontend artifacts (`.tsx`, Vite/Tailwind configs, UI component code) in backend.
- Enforce clear API error handling and input validation on request boundaries.
- Preserve backend boundary checks and avoid cross-repo file leakage.
- Prefer focused service-layer logic with thin route handlers.
- For GoHighLevel integration changes, verify current behavior against official GHL API docs before implementing.
- Keep temporary/debug/one-off scripts in backend `temp/` paths, not production source folders.
